Z||000000||2M4 Dale||08-14-2001||12:52 PM||||I am about to do a V6 swap into my 87 coupe. I have a brand new engine that has never been installed. It is a 1988 Fiero HO engine. I was wondering..has anyone ever scraped the stock fuel injection in lieu of a Edelbrock and a Holley ???? (scrap the computer) I was wondering how a traditional engine build would work ? How much power could I make with the carb as opposed to the Fuel injection. I plan to have my engine balanced and blueprinted and have the heads ported and run a cam with at least roller rockers and maybe a roller cam. I also am going to use headers with no cat "SHHHHH" and maybe some fancy pulleys...etc.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-14-2001||01:29 PM||||I thought about that once myself, but I think with that small a displacement a good 2 bbl would be plenty. You can use an old stock manifold too, when 2.8 were carbed. I dont know about distributor, dont it use computer to adjust timing. Maybe you could just use a carbed 2.8 dist or HEI. <P>BTW howd your cookout go, sorry couldnt make it but our club went to Canton Auto Museum. Maybe next time. You going to cincy? Oh and still looking for a nice V6/auto so no new kit being built yet.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||08-14-2001||02:08 PM||||The cookout was fun !!! We all had a good time. Maybe you can make it next year....I'm thinking about doing the Fairfield thing on Saturday but no promises yet. <P>If I were to use a 4bbl carb it would have to be a small one..I know. I don't know about the distributor though....anyone know ????????||||reg||1
